input.content:
Issue: Parent N7 (3b572cc, average 0.5544) answered its own open question in the negative and left the mechanism it named unbuilt: asked to write the entries the key does not carry "the way the memory writes its names", its check rewrote none of the ten the harness's own reading now settles, and every one of those ten was left exactly as the conversation wrote it. The parent's own run shows what that costs: at [[LawBench/conversations/0001/sample-0.json]] the answer `销售假冒注册商标的商品罪` stands against the gold `销售假冒注册商标的商品`, at [[LawBench/conversations/0003/sample-1.json]] `破坏电力设备罪` against the gold `破坏电力设备`, and at [[LawBench/conversations/0007/sample-1.json]] `...;持有伪造的发票罪` against the gold `...;持有伪造的发票` -- three samples whose whole residual is a title character the list never writes at the end of a name, and which the parent's model-driven check, measured on that run, did not touch. The reader of a name is mechanical, not a judgment: an offline pass over the parent's 99 readable LawBench answers (no model calls) finds 16 carrying an entry the list does not carry, and the list's own writing settles 10 of them; across the lineage's eight evaluated runs (781 LawBench answers, 2059 samples over the three tasks) the same reading rewrites 121 answers of which 1187 correct answers are never any, flips 40 from wrong to right and none from right to wrong.

Modification: the harness now writes the entries the answer key does not carry itself, from the list's own endings, instead of asking the model for them. `solver/tools/retrieval.py` factors the key's own strings out of `format_answer_key` into `listed_strings` and exposes them as `memory_listed_strings()`, so the pass reads the same authority the solver is shown (the key's budget included) rather than a list of its own; the rendered key is byte-identical to the parent's. `solver/passes.py` gains the reading: `listed_endings` takes what a written name of the list ends with -- the endings of the names the list's answers are divided into, which is what the memory's separators are for -- `piece_of_a_listed_name` leaves alone any name the list writes inside a name of its own, and `written_the_lists_way` drops the trailing characters the list never ends a name with, stopping as soon as the name it has is one the list writes, so a title or category word the list never uses comes off and nothing else does. `written_message` applies it to the reply's `final_answer` value alone, leaving the reasoning and the markup as they were. `solver/agent.py` applies it to the message the harness returns, after the model's check, and gates the whole reading on `memory_joiner()`: a memory whose answers are single strings (USPTO's 0/50 and Symptom2Disease's 0/200 joined answers) has no names to write out, so those two tasks are untouched by construction and no model call is added anywhere. No dataset name, label list or keyword list is used, and no Val or Test label is fed back.

Results: {"evaluation_result": {"USPTO": 0.2167, "Symptom2Disease": 0.89, "LawBench": 0.52, "average": 0.5422, "status": "partial"}, "message": "A tie with the parent inside the run-to-run spread the lineage has measured (~0.03), and this run's LawBench is what moved it: 6 samples were lost to the provider's content filter against the parent's 1, and failed samples stay in the denominator as wrong, so LawBench scores 52/94 answered -- 55.3% on the conversations that were answered, which is exactly what the parent's own reading of those same conversations would have scored. The mechanism was neutral in this run's material rather than harmful: it rewrote 8 of the 94 answers, all of them already wrong, flipped none and broke none. It had no room because the conversation wrote the three questions it was built for correctly this time ([[LawBench/conversations/0001/sample-0.json]] and sample-1 `销售假冒注册商标的商品`, [[LawBench/conversations/0003/sample-0.json]] and sample-1 `破坏电力设备`, all four correct against the gold, where the parent's run carried the title character and lost them), while the two questions it did rewrite wanted charges the answer never named ([[LawBench/conversations/0040/sample-1.json]] `销售假冒注册商标的商品罪` to `销售假冒注册商标的商品` against the gold `生产、销售伪劣产品`, [[LawBench/conversations/0026/sample-0.json]] `非法运输毒品原植物种子罪` to `非法运输毒品原植物种子` against the gold's `非法买卖、运输、携带、持有毒品原植物种子、幼苗`). USPTO 0.2333 -> 0.2167 and Symptom2Disease 0.87 -> 0.89 are the one- and two-sample draws those tasks re-take at across nodes with byte-identical memory. The expected effect was therefore not achieved on this run's score, and the reason is the work the mechanism does is only reachable when the conversation writes a title the list never uses, which this conversation did not."}

